TEST 10 — Kernel A / Kernel B Convergence Check
Purpose:
Confirm that Kernel A (algebraic DE5 polynomial) and Kernel B (physically calibrated DE5 response) remain internally consistent across the full domain.
This ensures QMD v3.0 fulfills its defining purpose as a dual-kernel cross-verification model.
Procedure:
Evaluate Δη(τ) = η_A(τ) − η_B(τ) across:
    • τ = 0.40 → 2.00
    • qbits = {24, 32, 40}
    • pwm = {8, 10, 12}
Compute:
    • RMS deviation
    • Max deviation
    • Structural divergence index (SDI)
Acceptance Criteria:
    • RMS deviation ≤ 3.0%
    • Max deviation ≤ 5.0%
    • No sign flips in relative ordering (η_A ≥ η_B or η_A ≤ η_B must not oscillate)
